-- title:
--   Automorphism fixing the X₀(Mp) q-expansions is a diamond
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and set $N = Mp$. Write $F =$ `x1FunctionField N` $=$ `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ N`, an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the $q$-expansion model of the function field of $X_1(N)$), and let `x1FunctionFieldBar N` be its base change `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F`, namely the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of $F$ under the coefficientwise ring embedding `coeffEmb`, which applies $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to each Laurent coefficient. Let $\rho$ be an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `x1FunctionFieldBar N`. Assume that $\rho$ fixes every element of the form `coeffEmb` $(f)$ that lies in `x1FunctionFieldBar N`, where $f$ ranges over `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$. Then there is a natural number $d$ coprime to $N$ such that $\rho\,x =$ `diamondAutBar N d` $x$ for all $x$ in `x1FunctionFieldBar N`, where `diamondAutBar N d` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the chosen automorphism `diamondAut N d` of $F$ satisfying `IsDiamondAut N d`.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement for the covering $X_1(N) \to X_0(N)$ in $q$-expansion form: the extension $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_1(N))/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(N))$ is Galois with group generated by the diamond operators, so an automorphism over the base field is one of them. It is used in the analysis of the level-$p$ structure at $N = Mp$, where the Atkin–Lehner involution has to be transposed against $U_p$ up to a diamond operator.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_coprime_forall_eq_diamondAutBar_of_forall_apply_coeffEmb_modularFunctionFieldFull_eq_x1FunctionFieldBar.lean

